msgid "not built — the models it exists for are not built"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:373 4d8e35e3e2494b5cad4b348e90265d52
msgid ""
"`Engine.model` is carried but only `MODEL_BLACK_SCHOLES` is reachable, "
"since Heston, Bates and local vol are not built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:376 c080fc9ff7d7492293b2092ace5a5a87
msgid ""
"**American approximations.** QuantLib has three and they disagree in the "
"third decimal, so the client names one rather than inheriting a default: "
"`BARONE_ADESI_WHALEY`, `BJERKSUND_STENSLAND`, `JU_QUADRATIC`. Omitting it"
" is `UNSPECIFIED_ENUM` on `engine.analytic.approximation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:381 c4a30e57ccae44beae1ee34dfadec889
msgid ""
"**Lattice trees.** Seven compile for a vanilla — `COX_ROSS_RUBINSTEIN`, "
"`JARROW_RUDD`, `ADDITIVE_EQUIPROBABILITIES`, `TRIGEORGIS`, `TIAN`, "
"`LEISEN_REIMER`, `JOSHI4`. A barrier takes `COX_ROSS_RUBINSTEIN` only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:385 37953a54b1a74481a08ddacfd705400a
msgid ""
"**Finite difference.** `preset` is `COARSE` (100×100), `STANDARD` "
"(400×200) or `FINE` (2000×800), each of them Douglas with no damping. "
"`custom` — explicit `time_steps`, `asset_steps`, `damping_steps` and "
"`scheme` — works on the plain paths and is `UNSUPPORTED` under quanto. "
"All four fields are read: a custom grid that named a scheme and got "
"Douglas anyway would be a defect rather than a simplification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:392 e636923d7aa34b7f8804ef6b1a0838ab
msgid ""
"`scheme` has no default, for the reason the grid has none: two schemes "
"are two prices for one trade. Five of the six arms build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 262a4e7e5559448eb4d8c0676c459b24
msgid "`Scheme`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 12e2b7efcb2f49ef81b359d2c9e94eda
msgid "What it is here"
msgstr "在這裡是什麼"

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 0fb83f06f61943e6b0112cbec77f4d78
msgid "`DOUGLAS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 91ea2e90307246e6a58838bb79068f13
msgid "QuantLib's own default, second order. What to send with no opinion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 847a1378c64749ec819a2d7a9a539609
msgid "`CRANK_NICOLSON`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 67d369a74a8f4065bb35327f586a57b4
msgid "Douglas to within a bit in one dimension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 38184e02b5954503b7e327155751fc84
msgid "`CRAIG_SNEYD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md cd329de710f74b8da1550a07f63d559f
msgid "Douglas *exactly* in one dimension — there are no directions to alternate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md a49a2efa90554e50a5d73bdadd4a70b0
msgid "`HUNDSDORFER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 33c30c39a794463d8bf263bf196d3aa5
msgid "A different theta; differs from Douglas in the seventh digit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md b30cd2cb042642189a707e56b79381a9
msgid "`IMPLICIT_EULER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 7ee648fe2bde4dbab2386eb889aaf1d6
msgid "First order, unconditionally stable; differs in the third digit"
msgstr "一階，無條件穩定；在第三位數字就有差異"

#: ../../HANDLERS.md bd139ad948594fbcade7104a9060a8c6
msgid "`EXPLICIT_EULER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 162dea1a77784cd59305d723bda36712
#: 4946066c82374bc58b6fcca875f4a311
msgid "`UNSUPPORTED`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:404 671b541ca0ee4d4db8e09f0bee7dcbc3
msgid ""
"Explicit Euler is refused rather than offered because it is stable only "
"while the time step is small against the square of the asset step, and "
"the asset step belongs to a mesher QuantLib builds inside the engine "
"rather than to anything on the frame. An unstable run does not fail: at "
"100×200 this build answered 2.4e140 and at 400×200 a NaN. Implicit Euler "
"is first order too, with no such condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:411 9471fa24c93b42f398409cc3e99c51d7
msgid ""
"`damping_steps` are Rannacher's fix for the oscillation a Crank-Nicolson-"
"family scheme shows against a kinked payoff or a barrier — the first few "
"steps taken fully implicit. They are counted out of `time_steps`, so a "
"request with at least as many damping steps as time steps is "
"`INVALID_ARGUMENT`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:416 28cf9078ecb74c01846f78f422a2dc1d
msgid ""
"**Monte Carlo.** `seed` must be non-zero, because QuantLib otherwise "
"seeds from the clock and the same inputs would price differently on every"
" request. Give `samples` or `absolute_tolerance`, not both. Setting "
"`progress_every_paths` switches to the batched path, which is what emits "
"`Progress` frames and what lets a cancel stop the work rather than only "
"the waiting — and it **changes the answer**, because batches draw from "
"the RNG stream differently from one run of the same total. "
"Reproducibility keys on `(seed, samples, progress_every_paths)`, which is"
" why `PriceResult` echoes the whole `Engine` message back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:426 ecad1c170ca541e29dea7ce32c60083b
msgid "Results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:428 4bb7779a2cd3439fad3f33887f5c2633
msgid ""
"`PriceResult.npv` always. `results` is a `map<string, Value>` keyed by "
"QuantLib's own name for each `ResultKind` named in `PriceRequest.results`"
" — `RESULT_KIND_DELTA` comes back under `delta` and "
"`RESULT_KIND_THETA_PER_DAY` under `thetaPerDay`, so a client asking by "
"kind and a client dumping an engine's `additionalResults` read one "
"vocabulary. Nineteen are mapped:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:434 e243ba0871334592b3599af12deada5c
msgid ""
"`NPV`, `DELTA`, `GAMMA`, `THETA`, `VEGA`, `RHO`, `DIVIDEND_RHO`, "
"`THETA_PER_DAY`, `DELTA_FORWARD`, `ELASTICITY`, `STRIKE_SENSITIVITY`, "
"`ITM_CASH_PROBABILITY`, `IMPLIED_VOLATILITY`, `QRHO`, `QVEGA`, `QLAMBDA`,"
" `FAIR_RATE`, `LEG_NPV`, `LEG_BPS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:439 f6c2054b2a60425397a4c97fb77582f1
msgid ""
"`IMPLIED_VOLATILITY` is the one that takes an input of its own. It is a "
"root find, not a published result, so `PriceRequest.implied_volatility` "
"carries the price to invert and, optionally, the bracket and tolerance to"
" look in; without a target the request is `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, because "
"inverting the price the request is about to compute would hand back the "
"volatility the client sent. QuantLib can invert a vanilla, a barrier and "
"a double barrier; asked of any other style the kind comes back in "
"`unavailable_results` like any other result an engine cannot supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:448 24a6c849a59e4f71902f82febf9961ab
msgid ""
"Anything else in the enum — the bond, credit and remaining cash-flow "
"kinds — is `UNSUPPORTED`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:451 6d752fe90d824a8db420457ffcf9731f
msgid ""
"An engine that cannot supply a result you asked for **names the "
"absence**: the kind comes back in `PriceResult.unavailable_results` and "
"the price comes back with it. Refusing the whole request would cost the "
"price too, and a client that wanted the NPV would learn to ask for "
"nothing. `AnalyticEuropeanEngine` has vega and the binomial one does not;"
" a frontend should be able to ask both the same question and be told "
"which answered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:458 d2c47760d973409fa07f090f8631bec3
msgid ""
"The same field carries a kind that does not apply to the instrument at "
"all — a fair rate asked of an option, a greek asked of a swap. A kind "
"this build does not implement anywhere is a different matter, and `Hello`"
" answers that before the request is sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:463 ae842009e3444b4ab8708f5a9fe8e446
msgid ""
"`include_additional_results` returns whatever the engine published in its"
" own `additionalResults` map. Every value this layer reports is a "
"**scalar** — the vector and matrix arms of `Value` are not filled. "
"`error_estimate` is populated whenever the engine has one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:468 de77cc11442549f2a0fea7b84bc26cb6
msgid ""
"`include_cashflows` is served for the cash-flow instruments, which today "
"means swaps. Each row carries its payment date, amount, the discount the "
"engine used and their product, so the **sum of the present-value column "
"is the NPV** — that property is what makes the table worth showing rather"
" than decorating, and `test/smoke_v2.py` checks it. Coupons add their "
"accrual dates, notional and rate; floating coupons add the fixing date, "
"the spread and the gearing, and say whether the fixing came from "
"`IndexManager` or is still a forecast. Rows that have already been paid "
"are left out. Asked of an **option** it is `UNSUPPORTED`: an empty table "
"would read as an instrument that happens to have no cash flows rather "
"than one that was never going to have any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md:479 564880e4cf6a428187939754afa8e0b6
msgid ""
"`curve_samples` is served. Each entry names a market object and a "
"quantity and comes back as a `Series` on the result, sampled from the "
"very handle the engine priced against — which is the point of it: the "
"alternative is shipping the term structure and re-implementing QuantLib's"
" interpolation in the client, which is how a frontend ends up drawing a "
"curve the backend did not price with. A sample may ask for at most "
"`Capabilities.max_curve_sample_points` points, on "
"`curve_samples[n].dates` or `.times`: each point is a term-structure "
"query on the live graph, and a chart shows hundreds. Four quantities are "
"built:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../HANDLERS.md 5e29d03307d14eceb598bedb0ba0198c
msgid "`CurveSample.Quantity`"
msgstr ""

